{"severity":"error","file":"errors/linear_never_used_2.march","start_line":20,"start_col":4,"end_line":20,"end_col":39,"message":"The linear value `st` was never used.\nLinear values must be consumed exactly once — did you mean to pass it somewhere?","code":"linear_never_used","fix":null,"labels":[],"notes":["`st` is role `Prod`'s place in protocol `Stream`: next it must send an `Int` to `Cons`. Take that step with `Stream_Prod.send_Msg_Prod_Cons_1`. This is the top of the protocol's `loop`: to go round again, pass it to a function that takes this state as a parameter."],"category":"LINEARITY"}
